Loading a process's image turns off every entry past it up to the end of those that grant user mode a right,
the fence among them, which leaves the core's hardwired entries open to the process.

Caught-by: fuzz-rp2350
Report: PMP CSRs grant rights the slots do not

diff --git a/kernel/process.c b/kernel/process.c
--- a/kernel/process.c
+++ b/kernel/process.c
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ void process_activate(struct process *proc)
 {
     const struct pmp_image *img = &proc->pmp;
     struct core *core = core_self();
-    pmp_load(img->addr, img->cfg, img->count, core->pmp_loaded);
+    pmp_load(img->addr, img->cfg, img->count, pmp_entry_end);
     core->pmp_loaded = (uint8_t)img->count;
 }
 
